# ── secrets: NEVER commit ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The TLS private key is EMBED_TXTFILES'd into the app image, so the build
# artifacts below are secret-bearing too. Rotate anything that ever slipped:
# git history remembers, and a public push is a disclosure, not a mistake.
firmware/*/main/certs/
firmware/*/main/secrets.h
*.pem
*.key
secrets/

# ── build output (also contains the embedded key + OTA key + PMK/LMK) ───────
firmware/**/build/
firmware/**/build.*/
firmware/*/managed_components/
*.bin
*.elf
*.map
!firmware/mission/main/arms_84x104.bin

# ── per-machine config, not source ──────────────────────────────────────────
sdkconfig
sdkconfig.old
sdkconfig\ [0-9]*
!sdkconfig.defaults
dependencies.lock

# ── editor / OS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store

# ── generated page embeds ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Only the two personal.html encodings stay out: README step 4 regenerates
# them from assets/personal.html, and every builder replaces the page anyway.
# llms.txt / robots.txt / og.png / the favicon encodings SHIP - they are
# public-served content and og.png has no in-repo generator.
firmware/eth/main/personal.html.gz
firmware/eth/main/personal.html.br
# page_strip.bin is 12 MB of baked RGB565 and regenerates from the live page
# (firmware/mission/render_page_asset.py); the 4-line header it emits ships,
# so a fresh clone compiles before its first render.
firmware/mission/main/page_strip.bin
docs/**/diagrams/_*.html
docs/**/diagrams/_*.png

# ── stray tool venvs (regenerate: python3 -m venv, pip install matplotlib) ──
docs/**/diagvenv/
**/venv/

# ── personal/ stays local ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The archive (raw logs, superseded drafts, ops evidence with the flat's real
# LAN addresses, retired diagrams and their render scripts) and the writing
# live under personal/ and never ship. The public repo is the live docs +
# firmware + tools only.
personal/
